# Which of the contract gate's files are main's, and from which commit (#98).
#
# Read by scripts/contract-identity.sh, which `make contract-identity` runs and
# the required `compat guard` CI job runs on every pull request into this line.
# Every file in this directory, and every file in main's tools/contractdrift at
# the pinned commit, must have exactly one line below, or the check fails --
# a file nothing classifies is a file nothing compares.
#
#   pin <sha>        main's commit the copies are taken from. Forty hex digits,
#                    and it must be on main: a pin into this branch's own history
#                    would compare the copies with themselves.
#   identical <f>    byte-for-byte main's file at the pin. The check fails on any
#                    difference. These are the files that never name the SDK --
#                    the spec, coverage and error-registry readers, the checks,
#                    and the command -- so nothing about this line's dialect can
#                    justify a difference, and a difference is divergence. Which
#                    files must be here is DERIVED by the script, not taken from
#                    this list: every Go file that imports no SDK package at the
#                    pin, so a file cannot leave this class by being relabelled.
#                    A fix to one of them lands on main FIRST and arrives here by
#                    advancing the pin; editing the copy here fails the check.
#   advisory <f>     this line's own version of main's file. It differs by
#                    design -- drivers.go is written against this line's surface,
#                    conformance.go and the tests name the SDK -- so no machine
#                    can decide whether a difference is right. `make
#                    contract-report` prints each diff against the pin, and
#                    docs/release.md has a human read it before a tag.
#   own <f>          exists here and not at the pin: this file, and the tests
#                    that prove `make contract-check` itself fails (#98's
#                    acceptance), which main has no counterpart for.
#
# WHY A PIN, and not main's tip. Fetching the tip would let an unchanged commit
# on this line turn red because someone merged a formatting change on main that
# morning -- and a required check that flakes on another branch's schedule is one
# people work around by editing the copy, which is the divergence this exists to
# stop. Advancing the pin is a reviewable change on this line, made by a pull
# request that copies main's newer files in the same commit.
#
# 5e40964 is the commit the whole parity epic (#88) ports from.

pin 5e409641e3dfafb83227e02efee3d8a50ec5602c

identical checks.go
identical coverage.go
identical gosdk.go
identical main.go
identical sdk.go
identical spec.go

advisory conformance.go
advisory drivers.go
advisory drift_test.go
advisory go.mod
advisory go.sum

own acceptance_test.go
own main.pin
